           </property>
          </widget>
         </item>
         <item row="0" column="0">
          <widget class="QLabel" name="extensionRatioLabel">
           <property name="text">
            <string>Extension length ratio</string>
           </property>
          </widget>
         </item>
         <item row="1" column="0">
          <widget class="QLabel" name="extensionDirectionLabel">
           <property name="text">
            <string>Extension direction:</string>
           </property>
          </widget>
         </item>
         <item row="1" column="1">
          <widget class="QComboBox" name="extensionDirectionComboBox">
           <property name="toolTip">
            <string>Direction in which the flow extension is added: along the direction of the centerline at the vessel end, or along the normal of the clipped boundary.</string>
           </property>
           <property name="editable">
            <bool>false</bool>
           </property>
          </widget>
         </item>
         <item row="3" column="0">
          <widget class="QLabel" name="transitionMethodLabel">
           <property name="text">
            <string>Transition method:</string>
           </property>
          </widget>
         </item>
         <item row="3" column="1">
          <widget class="QComboBox" name="transitionMethodComboBox">
           <property name="toolTip">
            <string>How the original vessel cross-section is blended into the circular cross-section of the extension, over the transition length set below. Ramp fades the two into each other with a smooth curve that is flat at both ends, so the extension leaves the clipped boundary and settles into the circular tube without a crease; linear fades them at a constant rate; thin plate spline warps the transition instead, which loses the finer features of a non-circular cross-section within the first few layers of the extension.</string>
           </property>
           <property name="editable">
            <bool>false</bool>
           </property>
          </widget>
         </item>
         <item row="4" column="0">
          <widget class="QLabel" name="transitionRatioLabel">
           <property name="text">
            <string>Transition length ratio:</string>
           </property>
          </widget>
         </item>
         <item row="4" column="1">
          <widget class="ctkSliderWidget" name="transitionRatioWidget">
           <property name="toolTip">
            <string>Length of the transition from the original vessel cross-section to a circular cross-section, as a fraction of the extension length. 0 makes the extension circular right from the clipped boundary; 1 spreads the transition over the entire extension.</string>
           </property>
           <property name="decimals">
            <number>2</number>
           </property>
           <property name="singleStep">
            <double>0.050000000000000</double>
           </property>
           <property name="minimum">
            <double>0.000000000000000</double>
           </property>
           <property name="maximum">
            <double>1.000000000000000</double>
           </property>
           <property name="value">
            <double>0.250000000000000</double>
           </property>
          </widget>
         </item>
         <item row="2" column="0">
          <widget class="QLabel" name="transitionToCircularCrossSectionLabel">
           <property name="text">
            <string>Transition to circular cross-section:</string>
           </property>
          </widget>
         </item>
         <item row="2" column="1">
          <widget class="QCheckBox" name="transitionToCircularCrossSectionCheckBox">
           <property name="toolTip">
            <string>Morph the cross-section of the clipped vessel end into a circle along the extension. Turn this off to keep the outline of the clipped end along the whole extension instead, so that the area distribution of a non-circular end is not altered - though a strongly concave end may then be hard to cap.</string>
           </property>
           <property name="text">
            <string/>
           </property>
           <property name="checked">
            <bool>true</bool>
           </property>
          </widget>
         </item>
        </layout>
       </widget>
      </item>
      <item>
       <widget class="ctkCollapsibleGroupBox" name="CollapsibleGroupBox_4">
        <property name="title">
         <string>Capping</string>
        </property>
        <property name="collapsed">
         <bool>true</bool>
        </property>
        <layout class="QFormLayout" name="formLayout_3">
         <item row="0" column="0">
          <widget class="QLabel" name="remeshCapsLabel">
           <property name="text">
            <string>Uniform cap mesh:</string>
           </property>
          </widget>
         </item>
         <item row="0" column="1">
          <layout class="QHBoxLayout" name="horizontalLayout_3">
           <item>
            <widget class="QCheckBox" name="remeshCapsCheckBox">
             <property name="toolTip">
              <string>Retriangulate the caps so that their cells are evenly sized and near equilateral, instead of the slivers a cap is closed with. Only the caps are remeshed: the vessel wall comes through unchanged, and each cap goes on sharing its rim with the wall.</string>
             </property>
             <property name="text">
              <string/>
             </property>
             <property name="checked">
              <bool>false</bool>
             </property>
            </widget>
           </item>
           <item>
            <widget class="QLabel" name="capTargetEdgeLengthLabel">
             <property name="text">
              <string>edge length:</string>
             </property>
             <property name="indent">
              <number>8</number>
             </property>
            </widget>
           </item>
           <item>
            <widget class="ctkSliderWidget" name="capTargetEdgeLengthWidget">
             <property name="toolTip">
              <string>Edge length a remeshed cap aims for. 0 (the default) sizes each cap after the surface around its own rim, so that a cap is meshed as finely as the vessel it closes and a cap on a small branch is not meshed like one on a large vessel.</string>
             </property>
             <property name="decimals">
              <number>2</number>
             </property>
             <property name="singleStep">
              <double>0.100000000000000</double>
             </property>
             <property name="minimum">
              <double>0.000000000000000</double>
             </property>
             <property name="maximum">
              <double>10.000000000000000</double>
             </property>
             <property name="value">
              <double>0.000000000000000</double>
             </property>
             <property name="suffix">
              <string notr="true"> mm</string>
             </property>
            </widget>
           </item>
          </layout>
         </item>
         <item row="2" column="0">
          <widget class="QLabel" name="modelFaceIdArrayNameLabel">
           <property name="text">
            <string>Face id array name:</string>
           </property>
           <property name="indent">
            <number>10</number>
           </property>
          </widget>
         </item>
         <item row="2" column="1">
          <widget class="QLineEdit" name="modelFaceIdArrayNameLineEdit">
           <property name="toolTip">
            <string>Name of the cell array that holds the face ids. &quot;ModelFaceID&quot; is the name SimVascular and its meshing tools expect.</string>
           </property>
           <property name="text">
            <string>ModelFaceID</string>
           </property>
          </widget>
         </item>
         <item row="3" column="0">
          <widget class="QLabel" name="capMethodLabel">
           <property name="text">
            <string>Cap method:</string>
           </property>
          </widget>
         </item>
         <item row="3" column="1">
          <widget class="QComboBox" name="capMethodComboBox">
           <property name="toolTip">
            <string>Shape of the mesh that closes each clipped end. &quot;Center point&quot; fans triangles out from the centre of the hole, &quot;Simple&quot; fills the hole with a flat polygon without adding points, and &quot;Smooth&quot; builds a rounded cap that follows the shape of the vessel at the cut.</string>
           </property>
          </widget>
         </item>
         <item row="4" column="0">
          <widget class="QLabel" name="capConstraintFactorLabel">
           <property name="text">
            <string>Cap roundness:</string>
           </property>
           <property name="indent">
            <number>10</number>
           </property>
          </widget>
         </item>
         <item row="4" column="1">
          <widget class="ctkSliderWidget" name="capConstraintFactorWidget">
           <property name="toolTip">
            <string>How far the smooth cap bulges out of the plane of the cut, following the shape of the vessel at the rim. 0 (the default) keeps the cap in the plane of the cut, like the other capping methods; larger values give a progressively more domed cap.</string>
           </property>
           <property name="decimals">
            <number>2</number>
           </property>
           <property name="singleStep">
            <double>0.100000000000000</double>
           </property>
           <property name="minimum">
            <double>0.000000000000000</double>
           </property>
           <property name="maximum">
            <double>3.000000000000000</double>
           </property>
           <property name="value">
            <double>0.000000000000000</double>
           </property>
          </widget>
         </item>
         <item row="5" column="0">
          <widget class="QLabel" name="capNumberOfRingsLabel">
           <property name="text">
            <string>Cap rings:</string>
           </property>
           <property name="indent">
            <number>10</number>
           </property>
          </widget>
         </item>
         <item row="5" column="1">
          <widget class="ctkSliderWidget" name="capNumberOfRingsWidget">
           <property name="toolTip">
            <string>Number of concentric rings of cells that make up a smooth cap. More rings give a finer cap mesh.</string>
           </property>
           <property name="decimals">
            <number>0</number>
           </property>
           <property name="singleStep">
            <double>1.000000000000000</double>
           </property>
           <property name="minimum">
            <double>2.000000000000000</double>
           </property>
           <property name="maximum">
            <double>30.000000000000000</double>
           </property>
           <property name="value">
            <double>8.000000000000000</double>
           </property>
          </widget>
         </item>
         <item row="1" column="0">
          <widget class="QLabel" name="labelModelFacesLabel">
           <property name="text">
            <string>Label mesh faces:</string>
           </property>
          </widget>
         </item>
         <item row="1" column="1">
          <widget class="QCheckBox" name="labelModelFacesCheckBox">
           <property name="toolTip">
            <string>Add a cell array to the output surface that tells the vessel wall and each cap apart by an integer id, for assigning CFD boundary conditions and for remeshing that keeps the face boundaries sharp. The wall gets id 1 and the cap of the first clip point id 2, the second id 3, and so on. If the input surface already carries face labels, those are kept: they are renumbered onto 1, 2, 3... and the wall and the caps follow after them.</string>
           </property>
           <property name="text">
            <string/>
           </property>
           <property name="checked">
            <bool>false</bool>
           </property>
          </widget>
         </item>
        </layout>
       </widget>
      </item>
     </layout>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item>
    <widget class="ctkCheckablePushButton" name="applyButton">
     <property name="toolTip">
      <string>Apply the clipping once. Check the button to automatically apply when parameters or planes change.</string>
     </property>
     <property name="text">
      <string>Apply</string>
     </property>
     <property name="checkable">
      <bool>false</bool>
     </property>
     <property name="checkBoxControlsButtonToggleState">
      <bool>true</bool>
     </property>
     <property name="SlicerParameterName" stdset="0">
      <string notr="true">AutoApplyPlane</string>
     </property>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item>
    <widget class="QLabel" name="clipStatusLabel">
     <property name="text">
      <string/>
     </property>
     <property name="wordWrap">
      <bool>true</bool>
     </property>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item>
    <spacer name="verticalSpacer">
     <property name="orientation">
      <enum>Qt::Vertical</enum>
     </property>
     <property name="sizeHint" stdset="0">
      <size>
       <width>20</width>
       <height>40</height>
      </size>
     </property>
    </spacer>
   </item>
  </layout>
 </widget>
